 R←Test_API_033(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;rc;msg;res
⍝ Runs "AddGitAttributes" twice. ⎕NPUT without a flag signals a FILE NAME ERROR when the file is
⍝ already there, so the second call used to crash - after the user had confirmed.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 tempDir←FilesAndDirs.GetTempSubDir'APLGit2-',⊃⎕SI
 res←1 G.AddGitAttributes tempDir       ⍝ "quiet", so nothing is asked
 →T.GoToTidyUp~FilesAndDirs.IsFile tempDir,'/.gitattributes'

 res←1 G.AddGitAttributes tempDir       ⍝ Again: the file is there now
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'already exists'⍷res
 →T.GoToTidyUp~FilesAndDirs.IsFile tempDir,'/.gitattributes'

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
